@baseUrl = https://api.businesscentral.dynamics.com/v2.0/67c998ad-883d-4441-8709-30a73ec72cb6/DK_Test/api/jkf/integration/v1.0/companies(45342618-9928-ed11-97e8-000d3a652983)
@token = REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN
@productionOrderId = REPLACE_WITH_ID_FROM_GET
@routingLineId = REPLACE_WITH_ID_FROM_GET
@routingEtag = REPLACE_WITH_ODATA_ETAG_FROM_GET

### Find order. Select the Planned/Firm Planned entry to release.
GET {{baseUrl}}/productionOrders?$filter=number%20eq%20%279363773%27
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Release the existing order using standard BC logic (WorkDate posting date).
### Already Released is a no-op. Simulated and Finished are rejected.
### Standard flushing rules apply. Number/SystemId may change on release.
### Follow the response Location or query productionOrders again afterward.
POST {{baseUrl}}/productionOrders({{productionOrderId}})/Microsoft.NAV.release
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Find released routing operations. Use the returned SystemId, not operationNo alone.
GET {{baseUrl}}/productionOrderRoutingLines?$filter=productionOrderNo%20eq%20%279363773%27
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Move the planned start. BC recalculates the planned end and related schedule.
### Example uses explicit Copenhagen winter offset; change the timestamp as required.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/productionOrderRoutingLines({{routingLineId}})
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: {{routingEtag}}

{
  "startingDateTime": "2026-11-16T08:00:00+01:00"
}

### Re-read to obtain the latest ETag and calculated timestamps before another PATCH.
GET {{baseUrl}}/productionOrderRoutingLines({{routingLineId}})
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Move the planned end. BC recalculates the planned start.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/productionOrderRoutingLines({{routingLineId}})
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: {{routingEtag}}

{
  "endingDateTime": "2026-11-16T16:00:00+01:00"
}

### Notes / sandbox validation before deployment
# These endpoints update existing records only. No tables/fields are added.
# Assign JKF PRODUCTION API in addition to normal BC manufacturing permissions.
# The routing API changes scheduled timestamps, not posted actual production time.
# Both timestamps can be sent in one PATCH only if standard scheduling preserves
# both. Otherwise the transaction fails and all scheduling writes roll back.
# BC standard validation can move related operations, capacity and component dates.
# Check release on a Firm Planned test order including its lines/components/routes.
# Check already-released no-op and rejection of Finished/Simulated orders.
# Check start-only/end-only changes, resulting timestamps and related scheduling.
# Check incompatible pairs, null timestamps and finished operations roll back.
# Check stale If-Match is rejected and read-only key fields cannot be patched.
# Compilation/runtime validation is pending: installed compiler requires .NET 10.
